From 64987f992afd70bdcf6e78c16c04192b35e6aec1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mohamed R. Khalil" <m.radwan.khalil@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 01:18:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(preemptive-compaction): keep the guard after a timed-out
 summarize, reject empty summaries

Four consecutive compactions in one 1M-window session failed with "Compaction
summarize timed out after 60000ms". Each request actually completed 64-67s in,
seconds after the plugin had already abandoned it, and one of them left a
summary message with no parts and no output tokens.

Because an abandoned attempt never latches the session, the next tool call
after the cooldown recomputed the ratio from the pre-compaction measurement and
started another compaction - one fired at a real fill of 71,333 tokens (7.1% of
the window) because the cache still held 824,748 from before the previous one.

- drop the cached measurement on session.compacted: it is the pre-compaction
  prompt, above threshold by definition, and must not justify another compaction
- verify the summary message carries text; an empty summary is logged, surfaced
  as a warning toast, and not latched, so a retry stays possible
- give the summarize call the same 120s budget the degradation monitor uses

Tests: three cases that fail without the fix (see
.omo/evidence/preemptive-compaction-refire-and-empty-summary/qa-report.md).
